{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"═══ LIVE NON-DEFAULT-PROVIDER EVIDENCE: every pass's model id, cited from the run's usage log ═══\n\nThis is the ticket's final [operator-attested] criterion: \"a real gate run **on the non-default\nprovider** shows the per-pass model ids actually used, cited from the run's usage log in a comment.\"\n\n**Run:** `rebar review-code --base HEAD~1 --head HEAD` (attested source) on commit 2e17171e5c, from a\nbuild carrying story b690's fix, `REBAR_USAGE_LOG` enabled. All three classes on **Bedrock**, while\n`cfg.model` stayed the bare direct-Anthropic default — so a dropped declaration is distinguishable by\nPROVIDER as well as model:\n\n    cfg.model = claude-opus-4-8              -> provider anthropic  (what a dropped declaration hits)\n    frontier  = bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8\n    standard  = bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6\n\n    step      op                                            model_class  model\n    ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n    base      code-review-base                              frontier     bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8\n    round_a   code-review-docs                              frontier     bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8\n    round_a   code-review-tests                             frontier     bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8\n    round_a   code-review-deletion-impact                   frontier     bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8\n    round_a   code-review-project-review-phase-boundaries    frontier     bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8\n    verify    code-review-verify                            standard     bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6\n    coach     code-review-coach                             standard     bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6\n    (none)    code-novelty                                  (none)       anthropic:claude-opus-4-8\n\n    verdict: PASS   llm_ran: True   llm_error: None\n\n**WHAT THIS SATISFIES.** All FIVE LLM-calling steps ran on the class the YAML declares, on a\nnon-default provider — `base` (`model: frontier`), `round_a`/`round_b` (`batch.model_ladder`),\n`verify` and `coach` (`model: standard`, `verify`'s landed by 172e). It also satisfies this ticket's\nsibling criterion \"no bare `claude-*` model id is resolved to provider `anthropic` during a run\nconfigured for another provider\" — for every classed step. The `round_b` step is absent from THIS run\nbecause Round-B membership is escalation-driven and the base reviewer recommended no overlays; its\ndeclaration is covered live by the anthropic run recorded on b690 and offline by\n`tests/unit/workflow/test_code_review_usage_attribution.py`.\n\n**WHAT IT DOES NOT SATISFY — stated rather than glossed.** The last row is a LEAK: the `code-novelty`\nsub-call ran on **direct Anthropic** while every classed step was on Bedrock. It is not a workflow\nstep (hence no `step`/`model_class`), it passes `config=cfg` with no class, and so it inherits\n`cfg.model`. So \"no bare `claude-*` resolves to anthropic during a run configured for another\nprovider\" holds for the STEPS but NOT for the whole run. Filed as **afeb** (parented to epic 061c)\nrather than folded in here, because it is a different seam — and it matters beyond this ticket: it\nmeans a Bedrock cutover (eb6e) is not actually complete, and it sends the diff and prior findings to\ndirect Anthropic.\n\n**A SECOND FINDING FROM THE SAME EXERCISE.** The first two attempts at this evidence used the\nCANONICAL Bedrock id form (`us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0`) and could not run at all:\n`_resolve_target`'s \"already provider-qualified\" test is `\":\" in model`, and a versioned Bedrock id\ncontains a colon in its version suffix, so the configured `provider = \"bedrock\"` was silently dropped\nand the id was then misread as `provider = \"us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1\"`. The gate\ndegraded to INDETERMINATE. Filed as **03b0**. This run therefore uses the UNVERSIONED aliases\n(`us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8`, `us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6`) as a deliberate workaround — worth\nknowing when reading the table above, because the evidence is real but was obtained around a bug.\n\n**PREREQUISITE NOTE.** This evidence was impossible before b690: the `step` and `model_class` columns\ndid not exist, and `op` alone cannot attribute a call to a pass. b690 is `LLM-Review +1` /\n`Verified +1` as Gerrit 1178 (not submitted — the stack lands when epic 061c closes)."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785622766002728001,"uuid":"ed611deb-b28e-4d48-b117-0fc56d1f6b2d"}